  "answer": "This feature request has been made before. Users have asked for a modifier key held while dragging, such as Alt or Ctrl, to switch to a second or other predefined layout. The maintainers closed those requests as duplicates of the umbrella ticket PowerToys#1411, which is the one to follow and add a thumbs-up to. Nothing like it is built in yet. What exists is a layout quick-swap shortcut, released in 0.35, which is Win+Ctrl+Alt+number. You can use it to switch layouts before you drag, but you can't switch while dragging with Shift held. The shortcut can't be customised. Until a hold-key or scroll-wheel layout switch is added, assign layouts to numbers in the FancyZones editor and use that shortcut."
 },
